<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    File Provider Paths Configuration
    
    CRITICAL: This file MUST exist for camera/file access to work.
    Referenced in AndroidManifest.xml FileProvider as android:resource="@xml/file_paths"
    
    Purpose: Defines secure file paths that can be shared with other apps
    Needed for: Camera photo capture, file storage, image sharing
-->
<paths xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    
    <!--
        External Storage Path for Camera Photos
        Allows the app to save and share photos taken by the camera
        Path: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.airportpro.app/files/Pictures
    -->
    <external-path 
        name="my_images" 
        path="Android/data/com.airportpro.app/files/Pictures" />
    
    <!--
        External Files Path (General)
        Allows access to app-specific external files directory
        Path: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.airportpro.app/files/
    -->
    <external-files-path 
        name="external_files" 
        path="." />
    
    <!--
        Cache Directory
        For temporary files and cached images
        Path: /storage/emulated/0/Android/data/com.airportpro.app/cache/
    -->
    <external-cache-path 
        name="external_cache" 
        path="." />
    
    <!--
        Internal Cache
        For temporary files stored in internal storage
    -->
    <cache-path 
        name="cache" 
        path="." />
    
    <!--
        Internal Files
        For app-private files in internal storage
    -->
    <files-path 
        name="files" 
        path="." />

</paths>

<!--
FILE LOCATION:
android/app/src/main/res/xml/file_paths.xml

FULL PATH STRUCTURE:
android/
└── app/
    └── src/
        └── main/
            └── res/
                └── xml/
                    ├── nfc_tech_filter.xml
                    └── file_paths.xml  ← CREATE THIS FILE

IF THE xml/ FOLDER DOESN'T EXIST:
1. Navigate to: android/app/src/main/res/
2. Create a new folder named "xml"
3. Create this file inside it

WHY THIS IS NEEDED:
Without this file:
- Camera photo capture will fail with SecurityException
- Cannot share files between app components
- Error: "java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Failed to find configured root"

WHAT EACH PATH TYPE MEANS:
- external-path: Full path to external storage root
- external-files-path: App's external files directory (Android/data/[package]/files)
- external-cache-path: App's external cache directory
- cache-path: Internal cache directory
- files-path: Internal files directory

SECURITY:
These paths are secure and only accessible by your app.
FileProvider ensures files are shared safely without exposing actual file paths.
-->